       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Thank you for looking into this, <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" data-account-id=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" accountid=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Jared Whiklo</a>. I was seeing this issue when running fcrepo4-vagrant from master... which was pulling an apparently bad war file from:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-exts/fcrepo-webapp-plus/releases/tag/fcrepo-webapp-plus-4.5.1-SNAPSHOT\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-exts/fcrepo-webapp-plus/releases/tag/fcrepo-webapp-plus-4.5.1-SNAPSHOT</a></p>\n\n<p>I have now updated the webac-audit.war file... and all is well. Sorry for the trouble.</p>\n\n<p>...Noting that fcrepo4-vagrant-4.5.0 fails as documented in this ticket.</p>",
